      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "> Thank you! I've built according to guide and when I try top inference it is failed with \"llama-cli: /home/ubuntu/bitnet/BitNet/3rdparty/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml.c:14652: void ggml_compute_forward_soft_max_f32(const struct ggml_compute_params *, struct ggml_tensor *): Assertion `!isnan(wp[i])' failed.\" have you faced such issue?\n\nllama-cli or llama-server?\n\nI got the same type of error, my issue is: https://github.com/microsoft/BitNet/issues/517\n\nOther users have experienced the same problem: https://github.com/microsoft/BitNet/issues/271\n\nIt's possible to fix it by adjusting the ubatch-size to 16, although my llama-cli works fine with ubatch-size at 32 on an Intel i7-8665U.\n\nAdjust the `command` variable in the `run_inference.py` file as follows:\n\n```python\ncommand = [\n    f'{server_path}',\n    '-m', args.model,\n    '-c', str(args.ctx_size),\n    '-t', str(args.threads),\n    '-n', str(args.n_predict),\n    '-ngl', '0',\n    '-ub', '16', # Changes batch-size to 16 instead of 32\n    '--temp', str(args.temperature),\n    '--host', args.host,\n    '--port', str(args.port),\n    '-cb'  # Enable continuous batching\n]\n```",
