      "body": "> llama-cli or llama-server?\n> \n> I got the same type of error, my issue is: [#517](https://github.com/microsoft/BitNet/issues/517)\n> \n> Other users have experienced the same problem: [#271](https://github.com/microsoft/BitNet/issues/271)\n> \n> It's possible to fix it by adjusting the ubatch-size to 16, although my llama-cli works fine with ubatch-size at 32 on an Intel i7-8665U.\n> \n> Adjust the `command` variable in the `run_inference.py` file as follows:\n> \n> command = [\n>     f'{server_path}',\n>     '-m', args.model,\n>     '-c', str(args.ctx_size),\n>     '-t', str(args.threads),\n>     '-n', str(args.n_predict),\n>     '-ngl', '0',\n>     '-ub', '16', # Changes batch-size to 16 instead of 32\n>     '--temp', str(args.temperature),\n>     '--host', args.host,\n>     '--port', str(args.port),\n>     '-cb'  # Enable continuous batching\n> ]\n\nyes,  llama-cli , probably because I run `run_inference.py`. Unfortunately nor 16 either 1 ub value doesn't change the situation.\n\nupd. `run_inference_server.py` behaves the same",
